NNAAMMEE
     iigg44 — Synopsys DesignWare I2C Controller

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines into
     the kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee iigg44
           ddeevviiccee iiiiccbbuuss

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           ig4_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iigg44 driver provides access to peripherals attached to an I2C con‐
     troller.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     iigg44 supports the I2C controllers based on Synopsys DesignWare IP that can
     be found in Intel(R) Core(TM) processors starting from the fourth genera‐
     tion, Intel(R) Bay Trail, Apollo Lake SoC families, and some AMD systems.

SSYYSSCCTTLL VVAARRIIAABBLLEESS
     These sysctl(8) variables are available:

     _d_e_b_u_g_._i_g_4___d_u_m_p  This sysctl is a zero-based bit mask.  When any of the
                     bits are set, a register dump is printed for every I2C
                     transfer on an iigg44 device with the same unit number.

